.docname {gol-bevy}
.include {docs}

**gol-bevy** is Conway's Game of Life as a native desktop app, built on the [Bevy](https://bevyengine.org) game engine. It runs on Linux, Windows, and macOS.

!(100%)[gol-bevy screenshot](media/screenshot.png)

## Features

- **Play, pause, and step** through generations, from 1 to 40 per second, or at ∞, maximum speed: as many generations as fit in each frame.
- **Draw, erase, and stamp** cells with the mouse. Stamps can be rotated and flipped before you place them.
- **Undo and redo** every edit, including rule changes and imports.
- **Any Life-like rule**: Life, HighLife, Day & Night, Seeds, or any rulestring in `B/S` notation.
- **Wrapping or fixed edges.** A wrapping board joins its opposite edges; a fixed board treats everything outside it as dead.
- **Boards up to 2048 × 2048**, independent of the window size or sized to fill it, with zoom and pan.
- **RLE import and export**, compatible with other Life tools such as [Golly](https://golly.sourceforge.io).
- **Keyboard and screen reader friendly**: Tab navigation, focus handling, and accessible names on every control.
- **Settings that persist**: board size, rule, edges, speed, grid, cell age, and theme are restored on the next launch.

